Project: /tmp/v5orch/w/t2 (Node/TypeScript, `npm test` runs node:test on test/*.test.ts). Fix exactly one bug in src/inventory.ts so the failing test "reserve can take the last units" passes.

Facts: reserve is:
  const have = stock.get(sku) ?? 0;
  if (have <= qty) { return false; }
  stock.set(sku, have - qty);
  return true;
Its doc comment says: "Takes qty units if that many are left; returns whether it did." The test asserts reserve('A1', 3) === true (A1 starts with 3) and then reserve('A1', 1) === false. The bug is the `<=` comparison: it should refuse only when fewer than qty units are left, so the condition should be `have < qty`.

Scope: edit ONLY src/inventory.ts. Do not edit any test file or any other file. Do not special-case tests. Keep the change minimal. When done, reply with the one-line diff you made and the output of `node --test test/inventory.test.ts` from /tmp/v5orch/w/t2.

Project: /tmp/v5orch/w/t2 (Node/TypeScript, `npm test` runs node:test on test/*.test.ts). Fix exactly one bug in src/checkout.ts so the failing test "checkout throws when out of stock" passes.

Facts: checkout's loop is:
  for (const [sku, qty] of skus) {
    if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { continue; }
  }
Its doc comment says: "Reserves every sku (throws 'out of stock <sku>' when one can't be), then returns the cart total." The test expects checkout(c, [['B2', 1]], 0) to throw an error matching /out of stock B2/. The bug is that a failed reserve is silently skipped instead of throwing. It should throw new Error(`out of stock ${sku}`) when reserve returns false.

Scope: edit ONLY src/checkout.ts. Do not edit any test file or any other file. Do not special-case tests. Keep the change minimal. When done, reply with the change you made and the output of `node --test test/checkout.test.ts` from /tmp/v5orch/w/t2. Note: checkout.test.ts's first test depends on src/inventory.ts, which another agent is fixing in parallel; if it fails only because of that, say so rather than touching inventory.ts.

